---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lessons = [
  {
    number: 17,
    title: "Screen Memory Intro",
    description: "Place characters anywhere using direct memory access",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 18,
    title: "Color Memory Basics",
    description: "Control character colors with rainbow effects",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 19,
    title: "Character Set Graphics",
    description: "Draw with PETSCII art and graphics characters",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 20,
    title: "Simple Sprite",
    description: "Create and display your first hardware sprite",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 21,
    title: "Moving a Sprite",
    description: "Animate sprites with circular motion",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 22,
    title: "Sound with POKE",
    description: "Generate notes using the SID chip",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 23,
    title: "Simple Music Sequence",
    description: "Play melodies using DATA statements",
    status: "available"
  },
  {
    number: 24,
    title: "Sprite Collision Detection",
    description: "Detect sprite collisions automatically",
    status: "available"
  }
];
---

<Layout title="Week 3: Graphics & Sound - Commodore 64">
  <style>
    .course-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff6b9d 0%, #c06c84 100%);
      color: white;
      padding: var(--space-12) var(--space-4);
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .course-title {
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
      font-weight: 900;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
      text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3);
    }

    .course-subtitle {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      opacity: 0.95;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
    }

    .course-description {
      max-width: 700px;
      margin: 0 auto var(--space-8);
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
      opacity: 0.95;
    }

    .course-stats {
      display: flex;
      gap: var(--space-8);
      justify-content: center;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
    }

    .stat-item {
      text-align: center;
    }

    .stat-value {
      font-size: 2rem;
      font-weight: bold;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    .stat-label {
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      opacity: 0.9;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    }

    .content-container {
      max-width: 1000px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 0 var(--space-4);
    }

    .section-title {
      font-size: 2rem;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .intro-section {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid #ff6b9d;
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-8);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .intro-section h2 {
      color: #ff6b9d;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
      font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .intro-section p {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    }

    .intro-section ul {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      line-height: 1.7;
      padding-left: var(--space-6);
    }

    .intro-section li {
      margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    }

    .lessons-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    }

    .lesson-card {
      background: var(--color-surface);
      border: 2px solid var(--color-border);
      border-radius: 0.75rem;
      padding: var(--space-6);
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto;
      gap: var(--space-4);
      align-items: center;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: var(--color-text);
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .lesson-card:hover {
      border-color: #ff6b9d;
      transform: translateX(4px);
      box-shadow: 0 4px 12px rgba(255, 107, 157, 0.1);
    }

    .lesson-number {
      width: 50px;
      height: 50px;
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff6b9d 0%, #c06c84 100%);
      color: white;
      border-radius: 50%;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: bold;
    }

    .lesson-content {
      flex: 1;
    }

    .lesson-title {
      font-size: 1.25rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
      color: var(--color-text);
    }

    .lesson-description {
      color: var(--color-text-secondary);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.5;
    }

    .lesson-status {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--space-2);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      font-weight: 500;
      padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-3);
      border-radius: 9999px;
      background: rgba(255, 107, 157, 0.1);
      color: #ff6b9d;
    }

    .start-button {
      display: inline-block;
      padding: var(--space-4) var(--space-8);
      background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff6b9d 0%, #c06c84 100%);
      color: white;
      font-size: 1.125rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: none;
      border-radius: 0.5rem;
      transition: all var(--transition-base);
    }

    .start-button:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(255, 107, 157, 0.3);
    }

    .wow-box {
      background: var(--color-bg);
      border-left: 4px solid #ff6b9d;
      padding: var(--space-4);
      margin: var(--space-6) 0;
      border-radius: 0 0.5rem 0.5rem 0;
    }

    .wow-box strong {
      color: #ff6b9d;
      font-family: var(--font-family-mono);
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .lesson-card {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        text-align: center;
      }

      .lesson-number {
        margin: 0 auto;
      }

      .lesson-status {
        justify-self: center;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <!-- Course Hero -->
  <section class="course-hero">
    <h1 class="course-title">WEEK 3: GRAPHICS & SOUND</h1>
    <p class="course-subtitle">Screen Memory, Sprites, and SID Chip Audio</p>

    <p class="course-description">
      You've been using graphics and sound all along—now discover HOW they work! These 8 lessons reveal the C64's hardware secrets: direct screen memory access, hardware sprites that move smoothly anywhere, and the SID chip for sound generation. By the end, you'll understand the magic behind every C64 game.
    </p>

    <div class="course-stats">
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">8</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Lessons</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">15-20</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Minutes Each</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <div class="stat-value">100%</div>
        <div class="stat-label">Hardware Power</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Course Introduction -->
  <div class="content-container">
    <section class="intro-section">
      <h2>What You'll Learn This Week</h2>

      <p>
        Week 3 unlocks the C64's multimedia capabilities. By the end of these 8 lessons,
        you'll understand how to:
      </p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Direct screen memory access</strong> to place characters anywhere using POKE</li>
        <li><strong>Color memory control</strong> to create rainbow effects and visual variety</li>
        <li><strong>PETSCII graphics</strong> to draw using the built-in character set</li>
        <li><strong>Hardware sprites</strong> that move smoothly independent of the character grid</li>
        <li><strong>Sprite animation</strong> using trigonometry for circular motion</li>
        <li><strong>SID chip sound</strong> to generate musical notes and effects</li>
        <li><strong>Music sequences</strong> by storing melodies in DATA statements</li>
        <li><strong>Collision detection</strong> using hardware registers that detect sprite overlaps automatically</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="wow-box">
        <strong>Week 3 Goal:</strong> By Lesson 24, you'll have created a collision-reactive sprite system
        with music—combining graphics and sound just like professional C64 games. You'll understand the
        hardware architecture that made the C64 a gaming legend.
      </div>

      <p>
        <strong>Prerequisites:</strong> Complete Weeks 1 & 2 first! These lessons build on loops, variables,
        and DATA statements from previous weeks.
      </p>

      <p>
        <strong>Learning approach:</strong> Each lesson reveals how something you've already used actually works
        under the hood. You'll start with "You've been using this already!" and end with direct hardware control.
        Type the short examples (20-40 lines), modify values, and watch the C64's hardware respond instantly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- Lessons List -->
    <section>
      <h2 class="section-title">Lessons</h2>

      <div class="lessons-grid">
        {lessons.map(lesson => (
          <a href={`/commodore-64/basic/week-3/lesson-${String(lesson.number).padStart(2, '0')}`}
             class="lesson-card">
            <div class="lesson-number">{lesson.number}</div>
            <div class="lesson-content">
              <h3 class="lesson-title">{lesson.title}</h3>
              <p class="lesson-description">{lesson.description}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-status">Start →</div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Call to Action -->
    <section style="text-align: center; margin: var(--space-16) 0;">
      <h2 class="section-title">Ready to Start?</h2>
      <p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary); margin-bottom: var(--space-4); max-width: 600px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;">
        Ready to unlock the C64's hardware? Week 3 takes you from PRINT statements to direct memory control. You'll learn the graphics and sound techniques that made the C64 a multimedia powerhouse.
      </p>
      <a href="/commodore-64/basic/week-3/lesson-17" class="start-button">
        Start Lesson 17: Screen Memory
      </a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
